          {
            "typeName": "dsDescription",
            "multiple": true,
            "typeClass": "compound",
            "value": [
              {
                "dsDescriptionValue": {
                  "typeName": "dsDescriptionValue",
                  "multiple": false,
                  "typeClass": "primitive",
                  "value": "<B>Summary</B><BR><BR>This study examined how Dutch courts handled dismissal disputes between residents, their program directors, and their employers. Case law was collected using keywords like ‘arts in opleiding tot specialist’ and ‘opleiding aios’ via www.rechtspraak.nl and included till 31th of December 2024. The courts interpret the national General Directive on education regulations for residents in training to become medical specialists, and consider the standing of the conciliation board ruling in relation to a decision from the court. Courts may also reflect on reasons for dismissal, due process, and employee protection.<BR><BR>\n<B>Data description (Qualitative data)</B><BR><BR>\nDistrict Court (Kantonrechter/Rechtbank)<BR><BR>\nKtr. Haarlem 25 april 2007, ECLI:NL:RBHAA:2007:BA4098, nursing home physician<BR>\nKtr. Amsterdam 26 september 2008, ECLI:NL:RBAMS:2008:BF5195, plastic surgery<BR>\nRb. Utrecht 8 april 2009, ECLI:NL:RBUTR:2009:BI0557, general practitioner<BR>\nRb. Amsterdam 25 april 2012, ECLI:NL:RBAMS:2012:BW7157, general practitioner<BR>\nKtr. Oost-Nederland 29 januari 2013, ECLI:NL:RBONE:2013:BY9847, nursing home physician (resume fraud during application)<BR>\nRb. Oost-Nederland 18 februari 2013, ECLI:RBONE:2013:BZ1359, nursing home physician (resume fraud during application)<BR>\nRb. Rotterdam 20 maart 2013, ECLI:NL:RBROT:2013:BZ5510, psychiatry<BR>\nRb. Amersfoort 16 november 2022, ECLI:NL:RBMNE:2022:5386, insurance physician (reimbursement of residency costs)<BR>\nKtr. Zwolle 24 januari 2023, ECLI:NL:RBOVE:2023:336, occupational physician (reimbursement of residency costs)<BR>\nRb Den Haag, 24 augustus 2023, ECLI:NL:RBDH:2023:12734, occupational physician (reimbursement of residency costs)<BR>\nRb Midden-Nederland 13 december 2023, ECLI:NL:RBMNE:2023:6981, occupational physician (reimbursement of residency costs)<BR>\nRb Midden-Nederland 27 maart 2024, ECLI:NL:RBMNE:2024:1627, forensic physician<BR><BR>\nCourt of Appeal (Gerechtshof/Hof/CRvB)<BR><BR>\nCentrale Raad van Beroep (CRvB) 28 september 2006, ECLI:NL:CRVB:2006:AY9698, clinical pathology<BR>\nCourt of Appeal Amsterdam 20 april 2010, ECLI:NL:GHAMS:2010:BM1955, general practitioner<BR>\nCourt of Appeal of The Hague 5 april 2016, ECLI:NL:GHDHA:2016:823, nursing home physician<BR>\nCourt of Appeal of The Hague 10 juli 2018, ECLI:NL:GHDHA:2018:1680, addiction medicine physician (disturbed relations)<BR>\nCourt of Appeal Amsterdam 9 juli 2019, ECLI:NL:GHAMS:2019:2394, general partitioner (professional liability barrister)<BR>\nCourt of Appeal of Arnhem-Leeuwarden 29 oktober 2024, ECLI:NL:GHARL:2024:6657, psychiatry<BR><BR>"
                },
